{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/kodd/Nutri","sessionId":"d0a4426d-7a3e-4469-b77d-2093bf639a97","version":"2.1.31","gitBranch":"HEAD","agentId":"a9c8b0a","slug":"purring-mixing-harp","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are helping design a universal health tracking system. Users can create CUSTOM tracking items:\n\n**Item** (what you track):\n- name, type (input|output|context), value_type (number|boolean|scale|text|select), unit, options\n\nYOUR TASK: Explore the CREATIVE ways users might extend the system with custom items. Generate 30-40 creative custom item examples across different categories.\n\nFor each custom item:\n1. **Item definition** (name, type, value_type, unit/options)\n2. **Why someone would track this**\n3. **Potential correlations it might reveal**\n4. **How it extends beyond \"standard\" health tracking**\n\n**Categories to explore:**\n\n1. **Unconventional health markers**\n   - Things doctors don't ask about but matter\n\n2. **Mental/emotional states**\n   - Beyond just \"mood\" - granular emotional tracking\n\n3. **Environmental factors**\n   - Home, work, air quality, noise, light exposure\n\n4. **Social/relational**\n   - Interactions, isolation, conflict, connection\n\n5. **Productivity/cognitive**\n   - Focus, creativity, decision fatigue\n\n6. **Spiritual/mindfulness**\n   - Meditation quality, gratitude, presence\n\n7. **Habits and behaviors**\n   - Screen time, posture, breathing patterns\n\n8. **Life events**\n   - Arguments, wins, deadlines, travel\n\n9. **Consumption beyond food**\n   - Media consumed, information diet\n\n10. **Body signals people ignore**\n    - Things we feel but don't usually track\n\n11. **Cyclical patterns**\n    - Things that vary by time of day, week, month, season\n\n12. **Experimental/fringe**\n    - Things biohackers or researchers might track\n\nShow the flexibility of the system - it can track ANYTHING with the input/output/context model."},"uuid":"7c1cd98a-aae4-44f2-90dd-cc18ce1a90b8","timestamp":"2026-02-04T03:55:16.210Z"}
{"parentUuid":"7c1cd98a-aae4-44f2-90dd-cc18ce1a90b8","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/kodd/Nutri","sessionId":"d0a4426d-7a3e-4469-b77d-2093bf639a97","version":"2.1.31","gitBranch":"HEAD","agentId":"a9c8b0a","slug":"purring-mixing-harp","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01RV17pS6ieG9pzt6U75gb6u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Creative Custom Health Tracking Items\n\nThis exploration demonstrates the flexibility of a universal health tracking system that goes far beyond calories and steps. The `input|output|context` model combined with flexible value types can capture virtually any aspect of human experience.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Unconventional Health Markers\n\n### 1.1 First Urination Color\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Morning Urine Color\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Clear\", \"2: Pale Yellow\", \"3: Yellow\", \"4: Dark Yellow\", \"5: Amber\", \"6: Orange/Brown\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Hydration status before any water intake reflects true baseline hydration.\n**Correlations**: Energy levels, headache frequency, skin quality, cognitive performance, hangover severity.\n**Beyond standard**: Doctors ask \"do you drink enough water?\" — this provides objective data without lab work.\n\n---\n\n### 1.2 Dream Recall Vividness\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Dream Recall\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: None\", \"1: Vague fragments\", \"2: Some scenes\", \"3: Full narrative\", \"4: Lucid/hyper-vivid\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Dream recall correlates with REM sleep quality, which standard trackers estimate poorly.\n**Correlations**: B6 intake, alcohol consumption, stress levels, sleep timing, creative output the next day.\n**Beyond standard**: Sleep trackers measure movement — this measures subjective sleep quality dimensions they miss.\n\n---\n\n### 1.3 Fingernail Condition\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Nail Health Check\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Healthy\", \"Brittle/splitting\", \"White spots\", \"Ridges\", \"Yellowing\", \"Slow growth\", \"Hangnails\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Nails are a 3-6 month window into nutritional status — deficiencies show up here first.\n**Correlations**: Biotin, zinc, iron, protein intake; thyroid function; stress periods 2-3 months prior.\n**Beyond standard**: Non-invasive biomarker that reveals nutritional trends over months.\n\n---\n\n### 1.4 Ear Wax Characteristics\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Ear Wax Type\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Dry/flaky\", \"Wet/sticky\", \"Darker than usual\", \"Lighter than usual\", \"Excessive\", \"Minimal\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Changes in ear wax can indicate hormonal shifts, stress, or diet changes.\n**Correlations**: Fat intake patterns, stress hormones, certain medications, seasonal allergies.\n**Beyond standard**: A body signal people notice but never think to correlate with anything.\n\n---\n\n### 1.5 Voice Quality\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Voice Quality\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Clear/strong\", \"Slightly hoarse\", \"Cracking\", \"Deeper than usual\", \"Higher than usual\", \"Strained\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Voice changes can indicate hydration, acid reflux, hormonal cycles, or early illness.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, acid reflux triggers, menstrual cycle phase, allergen exposure, social isolation.\n**Beyond standard**: Early warning system for illness; vocal strain from too much/little social interaction.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Mental/Emotional States\n\n### 2.1 Emotional Granularity\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Primary Emotion\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Serene\", \"Excited\", \"Hopeful\", \"Content\", \"Anxious\", \"Irritable\", \"Melancholy\", \"Frustrated\", \"Overwhelmed\", \"Numb\", \"Restless\", \"Grateful\", \"Resentful\", \"Curious\", \"Bored\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: \"How's your mood?\" is too blunt. Distinguishing irritability from anxiety from frustration matters.\n**Correlations**: Blood sugar patterns, sleep debt, specific foods, social interactions, hormonal cycles.\n**Beyond standard**: Emotional granularity itself is a skill — tracking builds vocabulary and awareness.\n\n---\n\n### 2.2 Rumination Intensity\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Rumination Level\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Mind quiet\", \"1: Passing thoughts\", \"2: Recurring theme\", \"3: Can't let go\", \"4: Obsessive loops\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Rumination predicts anxiety, depression, and insomnia better than general \"stress\" scores.\n**Correlations**: Caffeine timing, exercise, unresolved conflicts, news consumption, sleep onset latency.\n**Beyond standard**: Captures the *quality* of thinking, not just mood — a precursor to mood changes.\n\n---\n\n### 2.3 Sense of Agency\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Feeling of Control\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Helpless\", \"2: Reactive\", \"3: Neutral\", \"4: Capable\", \"5: In command\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Learned helplessness drives depression; agency drives motivation and resilience.\n**Correlations**: Decision fatigue, deadline pressure, autonomy at work, physical energy, recent wins/losses.\n**Beyond standard**: Psychological construct that predicts burnout, depression, and life satisfaction.\n\n---\n\n### 2.4 Emotional Hunger vs Physical Hunger\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Hunger Type\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Clearly physical\", \"Mixed signals\", \"Clearly emotional\", \"Boredom eating\", \"Stress eating\", \"Social eating\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Distinguishing hunger types is fundamental to mindful eating but rarely measured.\n**Correlations**: Emotional states, time since last meal, specific trigger events, certain foods chosen.\n**Beyond standard**: Bridges nutrition tracking with emotional tracking — the missing link for many.\n\n---\n\n### 2.5 Imposter Syndrome Intensity\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Imposter Feelings\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Confident\", \"1: Slight doubt\", \"2: Moderate doubt\", \"3: Feel like a fraud\", \"4: Waiting to be exposed\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Affects performance, risk-taking, and mental health in high achievers.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, recent feedback, comparison triggers (social media), hormonal cycles.\n**Beyond standard**: A specific cognitive pattern that affects career decisions and wellbeing.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Environmental Factors\n\n### 3.1 Ambient Sound Level\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Background Noise\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Silent\", \"Quiet (library)\", \"Moderate (cafe)\", \"Loud (traffic)\", \"Very loud (construction)\", \"Variable/unpredictable\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Noise affects stress hormones, focus, sleep quality, and blood pressure.\n**Correlations**: Focus duration, stress levels, headaches, irritability, sleep quality if evening.\n**Beyond standard**: Environmental factor that's constant but invisible — we adapt but it costs us.\n\n---\n\n### 3.2 Natural Light Exposure\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Daylight Minutes\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"number\",\n  unit: \"minutes\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Light exposure governs circadian rhythm, vitamin D, and seasonal mood patterns.\n**Correlations**: Sleep onset time, morning alertness, seasonal depression, energy levels.\n**Beyond standard**: Most people have no idea how little outdoor light they get — especially remote workers.\n\n---\n\n### 3.3 Clutter Level\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Space Clutter\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Minimalist\", \"2: Tidy\", \"3: Lived-in\", \"4: Cluttered\", \"5: Overwhelming\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Visual clutter increases cortisol and reduces focus; reflects and affects mental state.\n**Correlations**: Anxiety, decision fatigue, productivity, overwhelm, depressive episodes.\n**Beyond standard**: The state of your environment both reflects and influences mental state.\n\n---\n\n### 3.4 Air Quality Perception\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Air Quality Feel\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Fresh/crisp\", \"Neutral\", \"Stuffy\", \"Dry\", \"Humid\", \"Smoky/polluted\", \"Allergen-heavy\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Air quality affects cognition, headaches, allergies, and respiratory health.\n**Correlations**: Headaches, concentration, allergy symptoms, sleep quality, energy levels.\n**Beyond standard**: Subjective perception matters even when sensors say \"fine\" — personal sensitivity varies.\n\n---\n\n### 3.5 Temperature Comfort\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Thermal Comfort\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Too cold\", \"2: Slightly cool\", \"3: Comfortable\", \"4: Slightly warm\", \"5: Too hot\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Temperature affects sleep, mood, and cognitive performance significantly.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, productivity, irritability, food choices (hot drinks, ice cream).\n**Beyond standard**: Objective temperature isn't the point — *perceived* comfort is what affects you.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Social/Relational\n\n### 4.1 Meaningful Conversation Count\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Deep Conversations\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"number\",\n  unit: \"conversations\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Social connection quality matters more than quantity; small talk doesn't nourish.\n**Correlations**: Loneliness scores, life satisfaction, sense of belonging, evening mood.\n**Beyond standard**: Distinguishes between being around people and actually connecting.\n\n---\n\n### 4.2 Physical Touch Received\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Affectionate Touch\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: None\", \"1: Brief (handshake)\", \"2: Moderate (hug)\", \"3: Extended (cuddling)\", \"4: Abundant\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Physical touch affects oxytocin, stress hormones, immune function, and wellbeing.\n**Correlations**: Mood, stress levels, sense of connection, immune function during cold season.\n**Beyond standard**: A fundamental human need that many people are deficient in but don't recognize.\n\n---\n\n### 4.3 Conflict Exposure\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Conflict Today\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"None\", \"Witnessed conflict\", \"Minor disagreement\", \"Heated argument\", \"Major confrontation\", \"Ongoing tension\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Conflict is a major stressor that affects sleep, digestion, and next-day productivity.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, digestion, next-day energy, rumination, stress eating.\n**Beyond standard**: Captures relational stress that \"stress level 1-10\" misses completely.\n\n---\n\n### 4.4 Social Energy Balance\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Social Battery\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Depleted\", \"2: Low\", \"3: Neutral\", \"4: Charged\", \"5: Overflowing\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Introverts and extroverts recharge differently — tracking reveals personal patterns.\n**Correlations**: Type of social interaction, alone time, quality of interactions, next-day sociability.\n**Beyond standard**: Not \"how much socializing\" but \"how did it affect your energy?\" — individual patterns.\n\n---\n\n### 4.5 Felt Appreciation\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Felt Appreciated\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"boolean\",\n  unit: \"yes/no\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Feeling valued is a core human need; its absence drives burnout and resentment.\n**Correlations**: Work satisfaction, relationship health, motivation, self-esteem trends.\n**Beyond standard**: Simple binary that captures something profound about daily experience.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Productivity/Cognitive\n\n### 5.1 Decision Fatigue Level\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Decision Fatigue\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Sharp\", \"1: Slight fog\", \"2: Avoiding decisions\", \"3: Analysis paralysis\", \"4: Can't decide anything\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Decision quality degrades throughout the day; tracking reveals personal depletion patterns.\n**Correlations**: Time of day, number of decisions made, glucose levels, sleep debt, next-day willpower.\n**Beyond standard**: Explains why you make bad choices at night — and when to schedule important decisions.\n\n---\n\n### 5.2 Flow State Achievement\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Flow States\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"number\",\n  unit: \"episodes\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Flow is peak human experience — tracking conditions that enable it is valuable.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, caffeine timing, environment, task type, interruption frequency.\n**Beyond standard**: Measures the *quality* of work, not just hours — a flow hour is worth ten distracted ones.\n\n---\n\n### 5.3 Creative Inspiration\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Creative Juice\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Blank\", \"2: Stuck\", \"3: Normal\", \"4: Ideas flowing\", \"5: Bursting with ideas\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Creativity fluctuates; understanding patterns helps schedule creative work.\n**Correlations**: Sleep stage quality, novel inputs, exercise, boredom periods, constraint levels.\n**Beyond standard**: Creativity isn't random — it responds to inputs you can identify and optimize.\n\n---\n\n### 5.4 Task Switching Friction\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Context Switching Pain\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Effortless\", \"2: Minor friction\", \"3: Moderate effort\", \"4: Significant struggle\", \"5: Couldn't switch\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Some days switching is easy; others it's agony. Understanding why matters.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, current task engagement, anxiety levels, stimulant intake.\n**Beyond standard**: Reveals when deep work blocks are essential vs when varied tasks work fine.\n\n---\n\n### 5.5 Procrastination Intensity\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Procrastination Level\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: On task\", \"1: Minor avoidance\", \"2: Active procrastination\", \"3: Elaborate avoidance rituals\", \"4: Complete paralysis\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Procrastination isn't laziness — it's emotional regulation. Patterns reveal triggers.\n**Correlations**: Task anxiety, perfectionism triggers, energy levels, task clarity, fear of failure.\n**Beyond standard**: Distinguishes procrastination types — each has different underlying causes.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Spiritual/Mindfulness\n\n### 6.1 Present Moment Awareness\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Presence Level\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Totally distracted\", \"2: Mostly in head\", \"3: Partially present\", \"4: Mostly here\", \"5: Fully embodied\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Mindfulness isn't binary — tracking gradations builds awareness of awareness.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, meditation practice, stress levels, screen time, nature exposure.\n**Beyond standard**: The meta-skill that affects everything — how present are you to your life?\n\n---\n\n### 6.2 Gratitude Moments\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Gratitude Sparks\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"number\",\n  unit: \"moments\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Gratitude is trainable; tracking makes it tangible and reveals what triggers it.\n**Correlations**: Overall life satisfaction, relationship quality, sleep quality, baseline mood.\n**Beyond standard**: Moves gratitude from abstract concept to measurable, improvable skill.\n\n---\n\n### 6.3 Sense of Meaning\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Meaning Today\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Pointless\", \"2: Going through motions\", \"3: Okay\", \"4: Purposeful\", \"5: Deeply meaningful\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Meaning predicts wellbeing better than happiness; it's the \"why\" of daily life.\n**Correlations**: Type of work done, service to others, creative expression, connection depth.\n**Beyond standard**: Viktor Frankl's insight made trackable — what gives your days meaning?\n\n---\n\n### 6.4 Inner Critic Volume\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Self-Criticism Level\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Self-compassionate\", \"1: Gentle\", \"2: Neutral\", \"3: Critical\", \"4: Harsh\", \"5: Brutal\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: The inner critic drives anxiety, perfectionism, and depression; awareness reduces its power.\n**Correlations**: Sleep deprivation, mistakes made, comparison triggers, hormonal cycles.\n**Beyond standard**: Makes the invisible voice visible — the first step to changing the relationship.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Habits and Behaviors\n\n### 7.1 Posture Check\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Posture Quality\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Upright/aligned\", \"Slightly slouched\", \"Hunched forward\", \"Twisted/asymmetric\", \"Lying down working\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Posture affects energy, mood, breathing depth, and chronic pain patterns.\n**Correlations**: Energy levels, back pain, mood (embodied cognition), breathing quality, confidence.\n**Beyond standard**: The body-mind link is bidirectional — posture both reflects and creates mental states.\n\n---\n\n### 7.2 Breathing Depth\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Breath Quality\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Deep/diaphragmatic\", \"Normal\", \"Shallow/chest\", \"Holding breath\", \"Sighing frequently\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Breathing patterns drive the nervous system; shallow breathing maintains stress.\n**Correlations**: Anxiety, focus, stress levels, energy, blood oxygen, panic attack frequency.\n**Beyond standard**: The most accessible lever for nervous system regulation, yet rarely tracked.\n\n---\n\n### 7.3 First Hour Activities\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Morning Routine Quality\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Intentional routine\", \"Relaxed start\", \"Rushed\", \"Phone first\", \"Work immediately\", \"Chaotic\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Morning routines set the tone for the entire day; patterns reveal what works.\n**Correlations**: Daily productivity, stress levels, evening mood, sleep quality that night.\n**Beyond standard**: Not *what* you do but *how* you start — the quality of the transition to wakefulness.\n\n---\n\n### 7.4 Eye Strain Level\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Eye Fatigue\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Fresh\", \"1: Slight tiredness\", \"2: Noticeable strain\", \"3: Need to rest eyes\", \"4: Headache/pain\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Screen time proxy that captures actual impact, not just duration.\n**Correlations**: Screen hours, blue light exposure, headaches, sleep onset difficulty, blink rate.\n**Beyond standard**: Measures the *effect* of screen time, which varies by content, breaks, and lighting.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Life Events\n\n### 8.1 Unexpected Events\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Surprises Today\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"None\", \"Pleasant surprise\", \"Neutral unexpected\", \"Unpleasant surprise\", \"Multiple disruptions\", \"Crisis\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Unexpected events, even positive ones, drain adaptive energy.\n**Correlations**: Evening fatigue, stress levels, flexibility/rigidity, next-day recovery needs.\n**Beyond standard**: Captures the energy cost of adaptation — even good surprises are still surprises.\n\n---\n\n### 8.2 Win/Loss Ratio\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Wins vs Losses\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Big win\", \"Small win\", \"Neutral\", \"Small loss\", \"Big loss\", \"Mixed\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Psychological momentum affects motivation, risk-taking, and resilience.\n**Correlations**: Self-efficacy, motivation next day, risk tolerance, mood trajectory over weeks.\n**Beyond standard**: Simple framing that captures success/failure patterns and their emotional weight.\n\n---\n\n### 8.3 Deadline Pressure\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Deadline Stress\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Nothing pressing\", \"1: Aware of upcoming\", \"2: Moderate pressure\", \"3: Time crunch\", \"4: Emergency mode\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Deadline pressure affects sleep, decision-making, and health behaviors.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, food choices, exercise skipped, caffeine intake, relationship tension.\n**Beyond standard**: Explains the cascade of poor choices that deadlines trigger.\n\n---\n\n### 8.4 Financial Stress Event\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Money Stress\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"boolean\",\n  unit: \"yes/no\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Financial stress is a major health determinant, yet health apps ignore it completely.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, anxiety, relationship conflict, health-seeking behavior, food choices.\n**Beyond standard**: Acknowledges that health happens in context — money stress is health-relevant.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Consumption Beyond Food\n\n### 9.1 News Consumption\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"News Exposure\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: News fast\", \"1: Headlines only\", \"2: Moderate consumption\", \"3: Extended reading\", \"4: Doomscrolling\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: News affects anxiety, worldview, and sense of agency; most people consume unconsciously.\n**Correlations**: Anxiety levels, sense of helplessness, sleep quality, mood, political arguments.\n**Beyond standard**: Information diet is as important as food diet — this makes it visible.\n\n---\n\n### 9.2 Social Media Emotional Impact\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Social Media Feeling\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Inspired\", \"Connected\", \"Entertained\", \"Neutral\", \"FOMO\", \"Compared/inadequate\", \"Angry\", \"Anxious\", \"Time wasted\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Not all social media is equal — tracking impact reveals personal triggers.\n**Correlations**: Specific platforms, time of day, who you interacted with, content types.\n**Beyond standard**: Moves beyond \"screen time bad\" to \"what specifically affects me how?\"\n\n---\n\n### 9.3 Learning Input\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"New Things Learned\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Nothing new\", \"1: Minor new info\", \"2: Interesting fact\", \"3: Meaningful insight\", \"4: Paradigm shift\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Intellectual stimulation affects mood, creativity, and life satisfaction.\n**Correlations**: Curiosity levels, creativity, conversation quality, sense of growth.\n**Beyond standard**: Learning is a human need — tracking reveals if you're getting enough.\n\n---\n\n### 9.4 Fiction vs Non-Fiction Ratio\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Reading Type\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"All fiction\", \"Mostly fiction\", \"Mixed\", \"Mostly non-fiction\", \"All non-fiction\", \"No reading\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Fiction builds empathy and relaxation; non-fiction builds knowledge. Balance matters.\n**Correlations**: Empathy levels, stress recovery, creativity, analytical thinking, sleep quality.\n**Beyond standard**: Reading type affects different cognitive and emotional systems.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Body Signals People Ignore\n\n### 10.1 Gut Feeling\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Intuition Signal\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Strong positive\", \"Mild positive\", \"Neutral\", \"Mild unease\", \"Strong warning\", \"Conflicted\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Gut feelings are rapid pattern recognition; tracking accuracy builds trust in intuition.\n**Correlations**: Decision outcomes, anxiety (vs intuition), blood sugar, sleep quality.\n**Beyond standard**: Distinguishes anxiety (generalized) from intuition (specific) over time.\n\n---\n\n### 10.2 Jaw Tension\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Jaw Clenching\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Relaxed\", \"1: Slight tension\", \"2: Moderate clenching\", \"3: Tight/sore\", \"4: Pain/locked\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Jaw tension is unconscious stress storage; awareness is the first step to releasing.\n**Correlations**: Stress levels, sleep quality (bruxism), headaches, neck pain, TMJ issues.\n**Beyond standard**: A body location where stress hides — tracking makes the unconscious conscious.\n\n---\n\n### 10.3 Libido Level\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Sexual Desire\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Absent\", \"1: Low\", \"2: Moderate\", \"3: Present\", \"4: High\", \"5: Very high\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Libido reflects hormonal health, stress, relationship quality, and overall vitality.\n**Correlations**: Sleep, stress, relationship connection, hormonal cycles, exercise, medications.\n**Beyond standard**: A sensitive indicator of overall health that people feel but rarely correlate.\n\n---\n\n### 10.4 Internal Temperature Sensation\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Internal Temp Feel\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Running cold\", \"Comfortable\", \"Running warm\", \"Hot flashes\", \"Chills\", \"Fluctuating\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Internal temperature perception reflects metabolism, hormones, and illness onset.\n**Correlations**: Thyroid function, menstrual cycle, early illness, caffeine, spicy food, anxiety.\n**Beyond standard**: Subjective temperature independent of environment — body regulation quality.\n\n---\n\n### 10.5 Tinnitus Level\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Ear Ringing\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"0: Silent\", \"1: Barely noticeable\", \"2: Noticeable in quiet\", \"3: Distracting\", \"4: Overwhelming\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Tinnitus fluctuates with stress, sleep, caffeine, and certain foods — patterns help management.\n**Correlations**: Stress, sleep deprivation, caffeine, sodium, certain medications, blood pressure.\n**Beyond standard**: For tinnitus sufferers, tracking triggers is life-changing; for others, early warning.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Cyclical Patterns\n\n### 11.1 Menstrual Cycle Day\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Cycle Day\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"number\",\n  unit: \"day\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Hormonal cycles affect energy, mood, cognition, and physical capacity throughout the month.\n**Correlations**: Everything — mood, energy, food cravings, social desire, pain tolerance, creativity.\n**Beyond standard**: Context that explains many \"mysterious\" fluctuations when correlated with other metrics.\n\n---\n\n### 11.2 Seasonal Affective Pattern\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Seasonal Mood Shift\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"scale\",\n  options: [\"1: Winter blues severe\", \"2: Noticeably affected\", \"3: Mild seasonal shift\", \"4: Season-neutral\", \"5: Thriving this season\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Seasonal patterns affect 10-20% of people significantly; tracking confirms and quantifies.\n**Correlations**: Light exposure, vitamin D, exercise outdoors, social activity, latitude.\n**Beyond standard**: Makes seasonal depression visible and validates the experience with data.\n\n---\n\n### 11.3 Circadian Energy Mapping\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Energy by Time Block\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Morning person\", \"Late morning peak\", \"Afternoon person\", \"Evening person\", \"Night owl\", \"No clear pattern\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Chronotype affects when to schedule demanding work, exercise, and social time.\n**Correlations**: Sleep timing, productivity peaks, exercise effectiveness, meal timing.\n**Beyond standard**: Personalized time optimization — when are YOU at your best?\n\n---\n\n### 11.4 Weekly Energy Pattern\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Day of Week Energy\",\n  type: \"context\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"Monday slump\", \"Building momentum\", \"Mid-week peak\", \"Thursday fade\", \"Friday relief\", \"Weekend different\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Weekly rhythms are real; awareness helps with scheduling and expectations.\n**Correlations**: Work patterns, weekend recovery, social obligations, meal patterns.\n**Beyond standard**: The week as a physiological unit, not just a calendar one.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Experimental/Fringe\n\n### 12.1 Ketone Level (Breath)\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Breath Ketones\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"number\",\n  unit: \"ppm\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Metabolic flexibility indicator; relevant for keto, fasting, and metabolic health.\n**Correlations**: Mental clarity, hunger levels, exercise performance, fasting duration, carb intake.\n**Beyond standard**: Biohacker metric that reveals metabolic state without blood draws.\n\n---\n\n### 12.2 Heart Rate Variability Context\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"HRV Feeling Match\",\n  type: \"output\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"HRV high, feel great\", \"HRV high, feel tired\", \"HRV low, feel fine\", \"HRV low, feel off\", \"Haven't checked\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: HRV doesn't always match subjective feeling — tracking both reveals personal patterns.\n**Correlations**: Actual recovery vs measured, stress perception, training readiness.\n**Beyond standard**: Correlates objective measurement with subjective experience — the gap is informative.\n\n---\n\n### 12.3 Supplement Timing Log\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Supplement Stack\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"text\",\n  unit: \"freeform\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Biohackers need to correlate specific supplement stacks with outcomes.\n**Correlations**: Energy, focus, sleep, any tracked metric — depends on supplements.\n**Beyond standard**: Enables N=1 experiments with personal supplement protocols.\n\n---\n\n### 12.4 Grounding/Earthing Time\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Barefoot Earth Contact\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"number\",\n  unit: \"minutes\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Earthing enthusiasts believe ground contact affects inflammation and sleep.\n**Correlations**: Sleep quality, inflammation markers, mood, pain levels.\n**Beyond standard**: Fringe practice that can be tested personally with data over time.\n\n---\n\n### 12.5 Cold Exposure\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Cold Exposure\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"select\",\n  options: [\"None\", \"Cold shower finish\", \"Full cold shower\", \"Ice bath <5min\", \"Ice bath 5-10min\", \"Ice bath >10min\", \"Cold plunge\"]\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Cold exposure affects mood, inflammation, metabolism, and resilience.\n**Correlations**: Mood boost, energy, inflammation, brown fat activation, stress resilience.\n**Beyond standard**: Hormetic stressor with trackable benefits — popular in biohacking community.\n\n---\n\n### 12.6 Fasting Window\n```typescript\n{\n  name: \"Fasting Duration\",\n  type: \"input\",\n  value_type: \"number\",\n  unit: \"hours\"\n}\n```\n**Why track**: Fasting affects autophagy, metabolic flexibility, and mental clarity.\n**Correlations**: Mental clarity, hunger patterns, energy stability, sleep quality, weight trends.\n**Beyond standard**: Time-restricted eating is mainstream now; tracking enables optimization.\n\n---\n\n## Summary: The Power of Input/Output/Context\n\nThese 40 custom items demonstrate that the `input|output|context` model can capture:\n\n| Type | What It Captures | Examples |\n|------|------------------|----------|\n| **Input** | What you put IN | Cold exposure, fasting hours, learning, supplements |\n| **Output** | What comes OUT | Energy, mood, creativity, body signals |\n| **Context** | The CONDITIONS | Environment, social situation, cycle day, events |\n\nThe value types provide flexibility:\n- **number**: Quantifiable metrics (minutes, hours, ppm)\n- **boolean**: Binary states (yes/no appreciation, conflict)\n- **scale**: Ordinal progressions (1-5 ratings with labels)\n- **text**: Freeform notes (supplement stacks)\n- **select**: Categorical options (hunger types, emotions)\n\nThis system can track anything a human might want to correlate with anything else — that's the power of universal health tracking. The correlations users discover will be personal and surprising, revealing patterns that no standardized health app would ever think to look for."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3238,"cache_read_input_tokens":8500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3238},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CXnMVtMZZjDvmLpQntBDA","type":"assistant","uuid":"58ab5805-8dda-49c5-9128-f80d17477f83","timestamp":"2026-02-04T03:57:28.738Z"}
